id: pm-n98pir
title: "An annotation edit accepts text copied from a strings_compacted read, so a read-modify-write round trip silently truncates the stored entry"
description: "Found 2026-11-11 on PR 1708 (a Greptile finding). To correct one timestamp, I read the newest pm-7zs0 comment with 'pm comments pm-7zs0 --json', replaced one word and wrote it back with 'pm comments pm-7zs0 --edit 270 --file <text>'. The default 3,000-token output budget had compacted that 900-character comment to a prefix ending in '…'. read_output reported strings_compacted: true and the page said truncated: true, but nothing stopped the edit, so the stored comment lost its second half. The same round trip is natural for notes and learnings, and for any agent that fixes a word in place. Duplicate check: searched output budget, compaction, truncation and annotation edit; pm-8eclqf, pm-gh1552 and pm-gh1478 (closed) bound and preserve reads, but none guards the write side of a compacted read."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,annotations,data-integrity,output-budget
created_at: "2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T01:36:40.542Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:18.566Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-12T23:24:18.566Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: An annotation --edit whose replacement text equals a compacted projection of the stored entry (a prefix ending in the compaction marker) is refused with a typed code naming the --output-budget unbounded or --limit read that returns the full text; Compacted strings in budgeted reads carry a marker the write path can recognise; Edits of genuinely new text ending in an ellipsis still succeed
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "Budgeted reads end a compacted string with the marker …[+N chars], naming the omitted code units, in both compaction walkers. comments, notes and learnings refuse an --edit whose replacement ends with that marker (annotation_text_compacted, exit 2, nothing written), naming the --output-budget unbounded read and the --file edit. A bare trailing ellipsis and appends still succeed."
expected_result: A read-modify-write edit of an annotation never stores a budget-compacted prefix
actual_result: "A one-word fix of a compacted comment, note or learning is refused with the stored text and history unchanged; editing the full text, a genuine trailing ellipsis and an append quoting the marker succeed; the annotation-compacted-edit spec covers all three collections"
dependencies[4]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
