  pm-gh1478,related,"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-gh1552,related,"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-7zs0,discovered_from,"2026-11-11T19:08:30.933Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T23:49:31.298Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review of the batch PR (P2), fixed before push: layered budgets compacted a string twice. An intent read (--for) compacts a title to its prefix plus marker; a tighter output or session budget then compacted that string again and counted the first marker as omitted source text, so the marker read 14 chars instead of 1760. compactExplanatoryString is now idempotent: a string whose marker starts within the kept prefix length is returned unchanged, and the read-output walker still reports strings_compacted for any string longer than the cutoff, including one an earlier stage compacted. A marker that sits past the kept prefix is source text, so that string still compacts. continuation-tokens and text-normalization specs pin both cases.\n"
  "2026-11-13T01:36:40.541Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1717 CodeRabbit (minor), fixed: the annotation_text_compacted recovery examples named only the item id, so after an edit against a non-default tracker (--pm-path) the suggested read and edit could address another workspace's item with the same id. The examples are now rendered with resolvePmCommandScopeArgs, so they carry the tracker scope the edit used (and --no-extensions when it was set); the spec pins the scoped commands.\n"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T21:55:16.402Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation (2026-11-12). Compacted strings now carry a recognisable marker: compactExplanatoryString in src/core/shared/text-normalization.ts keeps the Unicode-safe 240-code-unit prefix and appends the ellipsis plus [+N chars], where N is the omitted UTF-16 code-unit count. Both compaction walkers use it, so JSON, TOON and the context-intent path agree. readCompactionMarker recognises only a trailing marker with a positive count (tolerating trailing whitespace), so a bare ellipsis or a marker quoted mid-text is ordinary text. runAnnotationCommand in src/sdk/annotations.ts refuses an --edit whose parsed replacement ends with the marker, before taking the item lock: annotation_text_compacted, exit 2, nothing written, with details collection, entry_index and omitted_characters, and examples naming the --output-budget unbounded read and the --file edit. The guard covers comments, notes and learnings (one shared path, so CLI, SDK and MCP alike). Appends are not refused, because quoting a compacted read as evidence is legitimate. Contract change: compacted strings used to end with a bare ellipsis."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T23:24:11.363Z","harness:claude-code","A compaction marker is only a write-side signal if it cannot be ordinary text: a bare ellipsis is legitimate prose, but an ellipsis plus the omitted count is not, so the write path can refuse a truncated round trip without false positives and the reader learns how much is missing."
